# Infrastructure. 1900 = 100. Two parts.
# 1750-1980 follows the general index. The forum's canal, aqueduct, viaduct and tunnel prices
# were tested as a substitute and show no movement within a fixed specification, so nothing in
# the record supports a different path over that range; the fragments are tabulated in
# prices-forum-fragments.md and the test is in prices-infrastructure.md.
# 1980-2026 is the ONS output price index for new work: infrastructure, chained from three
# vintages, each linked on an overlap year:
#   1980-2011  BIS Construction Price and Cost Indices, Output Price Indices, Table 1 column 13,
#              2005 = 100. The sheet notes that the infrastructure index does not exist before
#              1980, which is why the join is at that year rather than earlier.
#   1996-2015  ONS interim construction output price indices, "New work" table, infrastructure
#              column, 2005 = 100.
#   2014-2026  ONS construction output price indices, "New work" table, infrastructure column,
#              2015 = 100; 2026 is the mean of January to September.
# Link factors: ONS interim / BIS at 1996 = 1.0334; current ONS / ONS interim at 2014 = 0.7981.
# The whole chain is then scaled so that 1980 equals the general index for 1980, which keeps
# the series continuous at the join. After 2026 the 2026 real level is held and tracks general
# to 2050.
# The index measures roads and bridges, not railway permanent way, earthworks, canals or docks;
# it is the nearest published measure and is used as a stand-in for those.
# Last updated: 2026-11-16.
