# Land. 1900 = 100. Country land is England; city land is the United Kingdom.
# No United States or other-country data is used.
#
# country land: England farmland values, all land types, 1900-2024, from the
# Savills long-run series. The source values are real, rebased to 2023; they are
# converted to nominal with the general index and indexed to 1900. 2025-2026
# hold the 2024 real level and grow with general; before 1900 the 1900 real
# level is held. Source: Savills Rural Research, "Historic average land value in
# England - all types", https://www.savills.co.uk/landing-pages/rural-land-values.aspx
# (chart data, consulted 2026-11-15).
#
# city land: UK residential land values. 1900-1995 use the JST Macrohistory
# Database UK nominal house price index (hpnom) as a land-price proxy; 1995-2025
# use the ONS series "Land underlying dwellings" (AN.21111, current prices).
# 2025-2026 hold the 2025 real level and grow with general; before 1900 the 1900
# real level is held. Sources: JST Macrohistory Database R6,
# https://www.macrohistory.net/database/ (UK hpnom); ONS, "Land underlying
# cultivation, buildings and structures estimates from 1995 to 2025",
# https://www.ons.gov.uk/economy/nationalaccounts/uksectoraccounts/adhocs/3709-landunderlyingcultivationbuildingsandstructuresestimatesfrom1995to2025
# (consulted 2026-11-15). The ONS series is a total value, not per dwelling, so
# the 1995-2025 growth includes the increase in the dwelling stock.
